**Knowledge, Research, Understanding & Decision OS — Master Spec V6.5.1**

**Architecture Hardening, Invariants, Evaluation & Implementation Readiness**

Freeze-Ready Master Architecture, Visual Learning Framework, Memory Model, Provenance
System, Provider Continuity & Execution Plan

Version 6.5.1 | Supersedes V6.5 as planning authority | Integrates Addenda V1-V5
(see prior version headers for full history), the V6.5 hardening pass, and a
V6.5.1 internal-consistency correction pass triggered by an external
architecture review that scored the document component-by-component and found
four real contradictions rather than mere design preferences. **V6.5.1 fixes
those four contradictions and adopts two of the review's structural
recommendations (a three-axis Frozen/Experimental registry; invariant tests
activated by their owning PR rather than tested prematurely). It introduces no
new subsystem, consistent with V6.5's own scope discipline.**

**OPERATING LAW**
Think naturally. Preserve reasoning outside provider context. Research claims instead
of trusting sources. Compile the smallest defensible mental model. Visualize only
when it improves understanding. Test understanding through meaningful use. Preserve
how beliefs change. Humans authorize decisions. Accepted ADRs cross into execution.
Frozen Phase 1.5 executes them. **Continuity state is ephemeral by default and must
be revalidated, never trusted on age.**

---

## 0. Document status and transition gate

V6.5.1 supersedes V6.5 as the current planning authority. An external review
scored V6.5 component-by-component (provenance 9/10, infrastructure restraint
9/10, the Frozen/Experimental concept 9/10, but internal contract consistency
7/10 and PR sequencing 7/10) and concluded: **not ready to implement unchanged**,
because two real contradictions existed between sections describing the same
entity, and PR-0A scheduled tests for invariants whose owning capabilities
didn't exist yet. V6.5.1 fixes exactly those things — the ADR lifecycle
(Section 25A was missing the DEPRECATED transition that Section 19A and Appendix
A both already had), the LearningPackage lifecycle (Appendix A's schema was
missing the `evaluating` status that Section 25A's diagram already had), PR-0A's
premature invariant tests (now scoped to the seven invariants actually
checkable from contracts alone, with the rest activated by the PR that
introduces their owning capability), and the Capacity Watcher's position in the
build sequence (moved off the critical path pending real evidence, per its own
honest-scoping section). **The review's verdict after these fixes: ready to
implement.**

> **Re-verify before trusting.** Every fact in this section is a timestamped
> observation, not a durable truth — per Section 9 and the freshness discipline in
> Section 29. Re-run the commands below before acting on any of it.

| Readiness | Last observed state | Verify with |
|---|---|---|
| `localReady` | TRUE | `npm run phase15:audit` |
| `publicationReady` | TRUE | `npm run phase15:audit` |
| `externalReady` | FALSE | `npm run phase15:audit` |

**Remaining Phase 1.5 gates (3, not 4 — "repeated live eval baseline" closed via PR #38):**

| Gate | Status | Blocking condition |
|---|---|---|
| Non-bypassable external production approval | IN PROGRESS | Required-reviewer rule added live to GitHub; observation file not yet updated to match; audit still reports failing |
| Known-good rollback drill | OPEN | Not yet scoped |
| Production promotion + verification | OPEN | Depends on approval gate above being real, not just configured |

