## 31. Phase 1.6 implementation PR sequence

{% mermaid_diagram src="/diagrams/mermaid/phase-1-6-pr-sequence.mmd" title="Phase 1.6 PR sequence" /%}
*Figure 12. Bounded implementation sequence after Phase 1.5 freeze. V6.5 inserts four hardening/evaluation increments (PR-0A, PR-0B, PR-3A, PR-5B). V6.5.1 moves the Capacity Watcher off the main critical path (dotted branch) per its own honest-scoping admission (29A.4: no real capacity event has demonstrated the need), and annotates which PR activates which invariant, since an invariant cannot be meaningfully tested before the capability it governs exists.*

| Increment | Primary deliverable | Exit evidence |
|---|---|---|
| PR-0 | Schemas, events, typed IDs, privacy/authority invariants. | Unit/schema tests; no UI change. |
| **PR-0A** *(V6.5.1, corrected)* | **Architectural Invariants (1A) registry, with tests for the seven invariants checkable from contracts alone at this stage — INV-001, INV-002, INV-003, INV-006, INV-007, INV-008, INV-010. Lifecycle State Machines (25A) encoded as transition guards. A contract-consistency test verifying Appendix A's schema enums, 25A's state diagrams, and this document's prose lifecycle descriptions cannot drift apart — added after exactly this kind of drift was found and fixed in V6.5.1 (ADR's missing DEPRECATED transition; LearningPackage's missing `evaluating` status).** | **Each of the seven currently-enforceable invariants has an automated test; an illegal state transition (e.g. editing an ACCEPTED ADR) is rejected; the consistency test fails the build if a schema enum and its state diagram disagree.** |
| **PR-0B** *(new in V6.5)* | **Event/Replay Semantics (26A): eventId-based idempotency, causationRef/correlationRef enforcement, replay capability for derived state.** | **Duplicate event delivery produces zero additional state transitions; a fixture deletes a derived projection and confirms replay reconstructs it byte-for-byte equivalent.** |
| **PR-0.5** *(V6.5.1, reprioritized — evidence-gated side track, not critical path)* | **Capacity Watcher: predictive usage monitoring, automatic switch trigger, both-capped terminal state, `beacon` UX for in-progress/switched/paused states. No longer blocks PR-1 onward — see 29A.7.** | **Gated on real evidence of repeated capacity interruption (29A.7), not scheduled by default. Until then: simulated capacity-warning and hard-cap scenarios (not live — see 29A.4) trigger correct automatic switch and pause behavior in isolation; unit tests for threshold logic; no UI change outside `beacon` CLI output.** |
| **PR-0.6** *(V6.1, corrected)* | **Task Classifier (29B.2) running in log-only mode; `TaskClassified` event emitted per WorkUnit; HarnessAdapter (29B.10) scaffolded behind the existing ProviderAdapter interface, wired to OpenCode with a Groq backend credential, but not in the live routing table.** | **Classifier output logged and comparable against actual provider used, for every WorkUnit, with zero change to execution behavior; adapter contract-conformance tests plus a harness-subprocess normalization test (parses OpenCode stdout into the shared AgentRun schema) — no eval-gated routing yet (29B.7).** |
| PR-1 | PromptObserved, classifier, ResearchThread, ProjectContextSnapshot. **Plus (V5): automatic, unconditional `ContinuationPackage` generation at end of every session, stamped with `observedAt`/`observedMainSha`.** — the freshness/revalidation half of provider continuity stays on the critical path immediately, independent of whether Capacity Watcher's predictive half ever ships (29A.7). | Terminal capture → durable thread. **Plus: a consuming session demonstrably re-verifies live state before acting on a `ContinuationPackage` older than `staleAfter`.** |
| PR-2 | Source/Evidence/Claim Ledger + contradiction/freshness. **Plus (V6.5): `SourceRecord.contentHash` (8A) populated on every source fetch. Activates INV-004 (V6.5.1: this is the PR where claim provenance becomes real, so this is where INV-004's test moves from PR-0A to here).** | Claim statuses reconstructable from sources. **Plus: two evidence records citing the same locator with different content hashes are never merged; INV-004's automated test passes against real Claims for the first time.** |
| PR-3 | UnderstandingVersion + Understanding Compiler. **Activates INV-005.** | Versioning and package compilation tests. **INV-005's test (addressability of version N after N+1 exists) passes against a real UnderstandingVersion for the first time.** |
| **PR-3A** *(new in V6.5)* | **Beacon Evaluation Suite (33A) scaffolded: at least one fixture per BEACON-EVAL category (ARCH, RESEARCH, UNDERSTANDING, CODE, REVIEW, LEARNING).** | **Each category has a runnable fixture against real Beacon task shapes; results structured so a future provider comparison has somewhere to write its findings — this PR does not yet require the comparison itself.** |
| PR-4 | Private /lab read projection. | Existing UI visual regression unchanged. |
| PR-5 | Visual Understanding Router + renderer shells. | Renderer/accessibility/reduced-motion tests. |
| **PR-5A** *(new in V6.2)* | **Explorable-first default in the Visual Understanding Router (Section 15); `LearningPackage` generation pipeline (17A) wired to `UnderstandingVersion`; Section 17B evaluation checklist implemented as a gate before a `LearningPackage` moves from `draft` to `evaluating` to `trusted`.** | **A `LearningPackage` cannot reach `trusted` status without passing `evaluating` and the 17B checklist; fixture concept run end-to-end from prompt to explorable output (Section 32 style).** |
| **PR-5B** *(new in V6.5)* | **Learning Evaluation Protocol (33B): baseline-vs-explorable comparison harness, prediction/retrieval/transfer checks wired to at least one real concept.** | **A single concept run through both arms (baseline, explorable) produces a comparable, recorded outcome — this is the fixture that could move "Explorable-first learning" from EXPERIMENTAL toward FROZEN on Section 1B's architecture axis, once enough of them exist.** |
| PR-6 | Decision Readiness + Decision Candidate + ADRRequested. | Cannot authorize execution without accepted ADR. |
| **PR-6A** *(new in V6.2)* | **ADR supersession contract (19A): `status`, `supersedesAdrRef`, `supersededByAdrRef` fields; immutability enforcement on accepted ADRs; automatic `LearningPackage` historicization when its source ADR is superseded (19A.3).** | **Attempting to edit an accepted ADR's content fails; superseding an ADR correctly sets both directional refs and historicizes the linked LearningPackage without deleting it.** |
| PR-7 | DecisionPackage → Phase 1.5 WorkUnit handoff. **Activates INV-011.** | End-to-end controlled execution fixture. **INV-011's test (bounded package, not full transcript) passes against a real DecisionPackage for the first time.** |
| **PR-8** *(V6.3, extended)* | OutcomeObserved/Retrospective + **three-site projection (24A) built via the shared monorepo/build-time-filter mechanism (24B): business, decisions, and learning sites each rendering correctly from the same canonical lineage. Activates INV-009 and INV-012.** | Production evidence can revise understanding; public projection sanitized; **all three sites reflect the same underlying ADR/LearningPackage state with no separate authoring step; one accepted ADR triggers a single build that correctly updates all three deploy targets, verified by a fixture that accepts one ADR and asserts its presence/absence per site's filter rule (24B.2). INV-009 and INV-012's tests pass against real projections and real outcomes for the first time.** |

> **THE RULE THIS TABLE FOLLOWS *(V6.5.1)*.** The PR that introduces a capability
> also activates that capability's invariant test. An invariant listed in Section
> 1A but not yet testable (because the entity it governs doesn't exist yet) is not
> tested prematurely against a stub built solely to satisfy the test — it waits
> for its owning PR, and this table states explicitly which PR that is for every
> invariant.

Each PR must run the inherited Phase 1.5 publication preflight and protected GitHub
checks. No large all-at-once Phase 1.6 branch.

